WEBVTT

00:00:02.400 --> 00:00:03.760
I hate you.

00:00:05.320 --> 00:00:08.000
♪ There's... ♪

00:00:08.080 --> 00:00:09.920
Nothing to see. Gather there.

00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:13.280
Anything I can do?
I am a scientist. Is there any problem?

00:00:13.360 --> 00:00:16.480
I didn't mean to interrupt.
He isn't a good swimmer.

00:00:16.560 --> 00:00:19.800
I think it's too soon
for him to be out here unsupervised.

00:00:19.880 --> 00:00:22.040
MR. RAY: I can assure you,
he's quite safe with me.

00:00:22.120 --> 00:00:23.280
MARLIN: I'm sure he is.

00:00:23.600 --> 00:00:26.680
But you have a large class
and he can get lost from sight

00:00:26.760 --> 00:00:28.640
if you're not looking.

00:00:28.720 --> 00:00:31.400
Oh, my gosh!
Nemo's swimming out to sea.

00:00:33.520 --> 00:00:34.640
Nemo!

00:00:36.240 --> 00:00:37.720
What do you think you're doing?

00:00:39.440 --> 00:00:40.800
You're going to get stuck

00:00:40.880 --> 00:00:43.720
and I'm going to have to get you
before another fish does.

00:00:44.600 --> 00:00:46.480
Get back here.

00:00:46.560 --> 00:00:49.000
I said get back here now!

00:00:50.240 --> 00:00:51.840
Stop.

00:00:51.920 --> 00:00:53.920
You take one more move, mister...

00:00:55.080 --> 00:00:58.320
Don't you dare.
If you put one fin on that boat...

00:00:58.400 --> 00:00:59.880
Are you listening to me?

00:00:59.960 --> 00:01:02.000
Don't touch the boa...

00:01:02.080 --> 00:01:03.080
Nemo!

00:01:03.440 --> 00:01:04.800
He touched the butt.

00:01:04.880 --> 00:01:07.680
You paddle your little tail back here.

00:01:07.760 --> 00:01:10.520
That's right.
You are in big trouble, young man.

00:01:10.600 --> 00:01:12.680
Do you hear me? Big...

00:01:18.280 --> 00:01:19.320
Aagghh!

00:01:19.400 --> 00:01:21.440
Daddy, help me!

00:01:22.120 --> 00:01:24.040
I'm coming, Nemo.

00:01:26.120 --> 00:01:27.600
Get under me, kids.

00:01:28.680 --> 00:01:30.360
No! Dad!

00:01:38.280 --> 00:01:39.400
Nemo!

00:01:43.240 --> 00:01:45.280
Nemo! Nemo, no!

00:01:46.560 --> 00:01:47.720
Nemo!

00:01:47.800 --> 00:01:48.960
Nemo, Nemo!

00:01:49.480 --> 00:01:50.480
No!

00:01:52.760 --> 00:01:54.080
No!

00:02:04.160 --> 00:02:05.920
Nemo, Nemo!

00:02:14.280 --> 00:02:15.880
(FRIGHTENED GABBLING)

00:02:16.160 --> 00:02:17.480
Hold on!

00:02:23.200 --> 00:02:24.920
(MARLIN PANTING)

00:02:29.880 --> 00:02:30.960
Oh, no.

00:02:31.400 --> 00:02:33.520
No. It's gone. It's gone.

00:02:33.640 --> 00:02:35.920
It can't be gone. No. No!

00:02:36.000 --> 00:02:38.160
Nemo! Nemo...

00:02:38.800 --> 00:02:40.480
Nemo!

00:02:40.560 --> 00:02:41.760
No.

00:02:43.400 --> 00:02:45.520
Nemo! Nemo!

00:02:45.600 --> 00:02:46.640
No.

00:02:46.720 --> 00:02:48.200
No. Please, no.

00:02:51.040 --> 00:02:52.200
No, no.

00:02:54.840 --> 00:02:56.360
Has anybody seen a boat?

00:02:56.440 --> 00:02:58.280
Please. A white boat?

00:02:58.360 --> 00:03:00.800
My son! My son!

00:03:00.880 --> 00:03:02.240
Help me. Please.

00:03:02.320 --> 00:03:03.680
Look out!

00:03:08.400 --> 00:03:11.040
Oh, sorry. I didn't see you, sir.

00:03:11.120 --> 00:03:12.600
Are you okay?

00:03:12.680 --> 00:03:14.320
-He's gone.
-There, there.

00:03:14.400 --> 00:03:16.080
-He's gone.
-It's all right.

00:03:16.160 --> 00:03:18.560
-It'll be okay.
-No, they took him away.

00:03:18.640 --> 00:03:20.240
I have to find the boat.

00:03:20.320 --> 00:03:22.880
-A boat? I've seen a boat.
-You have?

00:03:22.960 --> 00:03:26.000
-And it passed by not too long ago.
-A white one?

00:03:26.120 --> 00:03:28.240
-Hi. I'm Dory.
-Where? Which way?

00:03:28.320 --> 00:03:31.240
Oh. It went this way.

00:03:31.320 --> 00:03:33.560
-Follow me.
-Thank you.

00:03:33.640 --> 00:03:35.040
Thank you so much.

00:03:35.120 --> 00:03:36.600
No problem.

00:04:03.240 --> 00:04:04.280
Wait.

00:04:11.280 --> 00:04:15.360
Quit it. I'm trying to swim here.
The ocean isn't big enough for you?

00:04:15.440 --> 00:04:17.520
You got a problem, buddy?

00:04:17.600 --> 00:04:18.880
Do you? Do you?

00:04:18.960 --> 00:04:21.080
Want a piece of me? Yeah.

00:04:21.160 --> 00:04:22.720
I'm scared now!

00:04:22.800 --> 00:04:24.800
-Wait.
-Stop following me, okay?

00:04:24.880 --> 00:04:27.960
What? You're showing me
which way the boat went.

00:04:28.040 --> 00:04:31.720
A boat? I've seen a boat.
It passed by not too long ago.

00:04:31.800 --> 00:04:34.720
It went this way. Follow me.

00:04:34.800 --> 00:04:36.840
Wait a minute. What is going on?

00:04:36.920 --> 00:04:38.960
You already told me
which way the boat was going.

00:04:39.640 --> 00:04:42.240
I did? Oh, no.

00:04:42.320 --> 00:04:46.080
If this is some kind of joke,
it's not funny and I know funny.

00:04:46.160 --> 00:04:50.360
-I'm a clownfish.
-No, it's not. I'm so sorry.

00:04:50.840 --> 00:04:53.840
See, I suffer from
short-term memory loss.

00:04:53.920 --> 00:04:56.240
Short-term memory loss.

00:04:56.320 --> 00:04:58.200
-I don't believe this.
-No.

00:04:58.280 --> 00:05:01.760
I forget things almost instantly.
It runs in my family.

00:05:01.840 --> 00:05:05.080
At least I think it does. Uh... Hmm.

00:05:05.920 --> 00:05:07.440
Where are they?

00:05:12.040 --> 00:05:13.160
Can I help you?

00:05:14.080 --> 00:05:16.480
Something's wrong with you. Really.

00:05:16.560 --> 00:05:18.400
You're wasting my time.

00:05:18.480 --> 00:05:20.360
I have to find my son.

00:05:23.680 --> 00:05:24.800
Hello.

00:05:25.640 --> 00:05:26.880
Well, hi!

00:05:27.840 --> 00:05:29.400
Name's Bruce.

00:05:30.120 --> 00:05:32.160
It's all right. I understand.

00:05:32.240 --> 00:05:34.680
Why trust a shark, right?

00:05:36.240 --> 00:05:38.040
(LAUGHS)

00:05:42.880 --> 00:05:47.400
So, what's a couple of bites like you
doing out so late?

00:05:47.480 --> 00:05:49.440
Nothing. We're not even out.

00:05:49.520 --> 00:05:50.800
Great.

00:05:50.880 --> 00:05:55.320
Then how would you morsels like to
come to a little get-together I'm having?

00:05:55.440 --> 00:05:59.640
-You mean like a party?
-Yeah, right. A party.

00:05:59.720 --> 00:06:02.920
-What do you say?
-I love parties. That sounds like fun.

00:06:03.000 --> 00:06:06.560
Parties are fun and it's tempting,
but we can't because...

00:06:06.640 --> 00:06:09.120
Come on. I insist.

00:06:09.200 --> 00:06:11.640
Okay. That's all that matters.

00:06:15.120 --> 00:06:17.440
DORY: Look. Balloons. It is a party.

00:06:18.360 --> 00:06:22.480
Mind your distance, though.
Those balloons can be a bit dodgy.

00:06:22.560 --> 00:06:24.280
You wouldn't want one of them to pop.

